---
# Rationale for the skipped rules below is documented in
# docs/plans/ansible-ci-and-lint.md.
exclude_paths:
  - .venv/

skip_list:
  # Roles here deliberately share variables with each other and with
  # inventories (e.g. postgresql_configured is set in `postgres` and read in
  # `tailscale`; tamanu_central_ip, is_btrfs, bestool_installed_version cross
  # roles and are set in inventories). Prefixing every register/set_fact with
  # its role name would break that cross-role contract and force edits to every
  # inventory.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
  # Role directories use an established hyphenated naming convention
  # (tamanu-single-install, ebs-volume, msupply-install, ...) referenced
  # throughout the playbooks. Renaming the directories would break every
  # reference for no functional gain.
  - role-name
  # Ops playbooks legitimately carry long shell snippets and complex
  # conditionals; wrapping them hurts readability more than it helps.
  - yaml[line-length]
